 acquisitions, including Screenmedia, Hacksoft, and Inov8, have bolstered its expertise in these high-growth areas. Notable clients include Lloyds Banking Group, ScottishPower, Royal London, and Roche. David Tuck was appointed CEO in 2024, succeeding Chris Martin, with a mandate to accelerate growth and expand the company''s data and AI capabilities. The company continues to be headquartered in Dundee and has additional offices in London, Edinburgh, Glasgow, and Sofia, Bulgaria. Keywords: digital product development, mobile app development, artificial intelligence services, enterprise software, financial services technology, digital health solutions, energy sector technology, public sector digital services, user experience design, software engineering, cloud services, data engineering, technology consulting, agile development, digital transformation, platform optimization, DevOps, web applications, strategic innovation, regulatory technology', '["project management","customer relationship management","human resources","web & portal technology","application development & management","javascript frameworks","intelligence and analytics","recruitment marketing","javascript graphics","App Development","machine learning","source code management","continuous integration","human resource management system","content management system","SaaS","marketing automation","web tools and plugins","web analytics","database","containerization","online form builders","testing and qa","paas","website builders","dev tools","Venture Capital","corporate learning management systems","tag management","containers","productivity solutions","widgets","open source","devops","b2b","video players","communication and collaboration","corporate","ui frameworks","Breakout stage","design","operating systems & computing languages","it infrastructure","Subsidiary","maps","advertising","sales","Immersive Technologies","email marketing","big data processing","security","api management","software development